A mounted table hangs below nothing rather than below the CapTable capability it was mounted with,
so revoking that capability, or destroying the table's pool, leaves it mounted;
every capability to an object lies below its pool's own node.

Caught-by: fuzz fuzz-pmp8 fuzz-rp2350 fuzz-smp2 fuzz-work qemu-replay
Report: capability to an object is a root

diff --git a/kernel/process.c b/kernel/process.c
--- a/kernel/process.c
+++ b/kernel/process.c
@@ -153,7 +153,8 @@ int process_mount(struct process *proc, uint32_t index, const struct cap *table,
     }
     /* It hangs below the capability it was mounted with, as the first hangs below the one the process was made with. */
     proc->tables[index] = *table;
-    cap_attach(parent, &proc->tables[index]);
+    (void)parent;
+    cap_attach(NULL, &proc->tables[index]);
     return KERR_OK;
 }
 
